# comprehension-before-commitment

Before writing any code or making any architectural decision, build a complete mental model of the system: read all versioned plans up to the current version, trace every relevant logic path, identify all component interfaces, and understand how every piece fits together. Commitment (writing code, opening PRs, merging) on partial context produces implementations that violate existing contracts, miss edge cases, or duplicate logic already handled elsewhere.

## Procedures
- Read all versioned plan documents in order before writing a single line.
- Grep / read every file that touches the interface you are about to change.
- Trace the request/data flow end-to-end across all layers before deciding where to add logic.
- Identify every caller of any function or type you intend to modify.
- Only after the full picture is clear, commit to an implementation approach.

